      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Drain soaked cod. Poach in fresh water for 10 minutes. Drain, cool, and shred into flakes, removing all skin and bones."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Fry potato matchsticks in hot oil in batches until golden and crisp. Drain on paper and set aside."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat 3 tbsp oil in a wide frying pan. Soften onion and garlic for 8 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add shredded cod. Stir for 2 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Beat eggs and season lightly. Pour into the pan."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add half the crispy potato. Stir gently over low heat until eggs just set but still creamy."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Remove from heat. Fold in remaining potatoes. Top with olives and parsley. Serve immediately."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Eggs rubbery",
              "cause": "Overcooked or heat too high",
              "fix": "Remove from heat just before eggs fully set. They continue cooking in the pan."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Potato gone soggy",
              "cause": "All added before eggs set",
              "fix": "Add half with the eggs and keep the rest for last-minute folding."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Too salty",
              "cause": "Cod not soaked long enough",
              "fix": "Soak for a full 48 hours, changing water twice daily."
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The Portuguese relationship with salt cod is unlike any other country's. There are said to be 365 bacalhau recipes, one for every day of the year. Bacalhau a Bras is named after a street vendor or tavern keeper from Lisbon. The combination of salt cod, egg, and fried potato is found all over the country and in Portuguese communities worldwide. It is a staple of Portuguese Christmas and Easter tables."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
